From 0f996c3d5bf44257f3352c005ae317df5cac01a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakub Jelen <jjelen@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:28:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Update the upstream signing key

Replace gnu-keyring.gpg with guile-gnutls-keyring.pgp, the keyserver
copy of the key that signs releases
(B1D2BD1375BECB784CF4F8C4D73CF638C53C06BE), because sqv cannot use the
old keyring: its copy of the signing key is outdated. The other
certificates in it are dropped (570 certificates of other people). Its
Source line names the new file instead of
https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gnu-keyring.gpg, which is not what the file
holds any more.
The commands are in the comment above its Source line.

The current key is needed to verify the release signature with
openpgpverify (sqv), which checks that the key was valid when the
release was signed.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 gnu-keyring.gpg          | Bin 2772611 -> 0 bytes
 guile-gnutls-keyring.pgp | 264 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 guile-gnutls.spec        |   4 +-
 3 files changed, 267 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 delete mode 100644 gnu-keyring.gpg
 create mode 100644 guile-gnutls-keyring.pgp

diff --git a/gnu-keyring.gpg b/gnu-keyring.gpg
deleted file mode 100644
index 900b2643250a61b5705826db6ab8a033a923f9f9..0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
GIT binary patch
literal 0
